<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohamoud Ali Shire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohamoud Ali Shire was sultan of the Warsangali in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanaag">Sanaag</a> region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> in the early 20th century. He supported the Dervish movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</a> against British rule, and in 1920, after the defeat of the Dervishes, the British exiled him to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seychelles">Seychelles</a>. He was later allowed to return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, where he remained a respected traditional leader.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohamoud-ali-shire.jpg" alt="Mohamoud Ali Shire" width="308" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Somali Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultan_Mohamoud_Ali_Shire_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
